package Libraries.Fabrication.Slicing

/*
The Segment class is one piece of a slice outline: the line where a single
triangle of the mesh crosses a slice plane. MeshSlicer makes them and
ContourGenerator chains them into loops.

Each end lies on a triangle edge, recorded by the edge's two vertex ids
(lower id first) so that the neighbouring triangle's segment, which shares
that edge, can be found exactly. Segments run so the solid is on the left.
*/
class Segment
    /* The slice plane this segment lies on. */
    public integer planeIndex = 0

    /* The mesh edge the segment starts on (its two vertex ids, lower first). */
    public integer aLow = 0
    public integer aHigh = 0

    /* The mesh edge the segment ends on. */
    public integer bLow = 0
    public integer bHigh = 0

    public number x0 = 0.0
    public number y0 = 0.0
    public number x1 = 0.0
    public number y1 = 0.0
end
